Third-party material

The files in src/xjyutping/data/ are generated by tools/build-data.py of
the LaTeX package (https://github.com/Beyond3345/xjyutping-tex) and are
distributed under Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0
(CC BY-SA 4.0, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/), because
they adapt share-alike material. They are built from:

  * the LSHK Cantonese Pronunciation List of Characters for Computers
    (jyutping-table), Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 (CC BY 4.0);
  * rime-cantonese jyut6ping3.chars and jyut6ping3.words, Creative Commons
    Attribution 4.0 (CC BY 4.0);
  * CC-Canto, Copyright (c) 2015-17 Pleco Inc., and the CC-CEDICT Cantonese
    readings, Copyright (c) 2015 Pleco Software Inc., both Creative Commons
    Attribution-ShareAlike 3.0 (CC BY-SA 3.0), as distributed with Jyut
    Dictionary (https://github.com/aaronhktan/jyut-dict);
  * OpenCC HKVariants.txt and TWVariants.txt, Apache License 2.0;
  * readings of 640 characters from the book data of 粵音資料集叢 by 石見田
    (https://github.com/jyutnet/cantonese-books-data), published without a
    licence statement and used with attribution.

The 'fancy' and 'discord' tone symbols (TONE_MARKS in
src/xjyutping/__init__.py) come from Visual Jyutping
(https://github.com/VincentTam/visual-jyutping), MIT License,
Copyright (c) 2024 Vincent Tam.
